<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Bancoquia '96 net profit up.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Bancoquia '96 net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bancoquia, Colombia's eight-largest bank, said on Wednesday its net profit rose to 23.57 billion pesos in 1996 from 21.80 billion the previous year.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it would propose, at a shareholders' meeting set for March 3, distributing 14.17 billion of the 1996 profit in the form of a 40 pesos per share dividend.</p>
<p>Spain's Grupo Santander announced plans late last year to acquire a 51 percent stake in Bancoquia for $153 million.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
